ng and Physician Services Deficiencies","concept":"staffing","concept_label":"Staffing & supervision"},"cms-f0744":{"code":"F-0744","title":"Provide the appropriate treatment and services to a resident who displays or is diagnosed with dementia.","category":"Quality of Life and Care Deficiencies","concept":"clinical_care","concept_label":"Clinical care"},"cms-f0756":{"code":"F-0756","title":"Ensure a licensed pharmacist perform a monthly drug regimen review, including the medical chart, following irregularity reporting guidelines in developed policies and procedures.","category":"Pharmacy Service Deficiencies","concept":"medication","concept_label":"Medication management"},"cms-f0761":{"code":"F-0761","title":"Ensure drugs and biologicals used in the facility are labeled in accordance with currently accepted professional principles; and all drugs and biologicals must be stored in locked compartments, separately locked, compartments for controlled drugs.","category":"Pharmacy Service Deficiencies","concept":"medication","concept_label":"Medication management"},"cms-f0868":{"code":"F-0868","title":"Have the Quality Assessment and Assurance group have the required members and meet at least quarterly","category":"Administration Deficiencies","concept":"administration","concept_label":"Administration & records"},"cms-f0908":{"code":"F-0908","title":"Keep all essential equipment working safely.","category":"Environmental Deficiencies","concept":"environment_life_safety","concept_label":"Environment & life safety"},"cms-f0580":{"code":"F-0580","title":"Immediately tell the resident, the resident's doctor, and a family member of situations (injury/decline/room, etc.)  that affect the resident.","category":"Resident Rights Deficiencies","concept":"resident_rights","concept_label":"Resident rights & abuse/neglect"},"cms-f0842":{"code":"F-0842","title":"Safeguard resident-identifiable information and/or maintain medical records on each resident that are in accordance with acce